          "label": "annex reduction and counterexample"
        }
      ],
      "gap": "The worked boundary is missing. def:p15-regular-conditional-law asserts (regular-conditional-laws.tex lines 49-51) that the regular-conditional-probability special case (S=Omega, target sigma-algebra F_0, X the identity) 'needs an existence hypothesis on the outcome space itself', i.e. that a regular conditional law need not exist without a hypothesis on (Omega,F_0). No probability space (Omega,F_0,P) and sub-sigma-algebra G are written for which no probability kernel from (Omega,G) to (Omega,F_0) satisfies K(.,A)=P(A|G) a.e. for every A in F_0, and no argument for that necessity is written. The only support is the citation at conditioning-independence-and-information-w02b-p15-008.tex lines 235-239 to Durrett p. 214, which states nonexistence and credits Dieudonne (1948) without giving the example: a citation where a demonstration is owed. The countable-cocountable model (w02b annex lines 171-269) does not close it, since a regular conditional law (K_0) exists there (part (iii)). Owed: a written model in which no regular conditional probability exists, with its complete proof, or a written argument that establishes the stated need for a hypothesis.",
